<title>TAIWAN: Taiwan passes on 54,000-tonne U.S. soybean tender.</title>
<headline>Taiwan passes on 54,000-tonne U.S. soybean tender.</headline>
<dateline>TAIPEI 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Kaohsiung division of Taiwan's Breakfast Soybean Procurement Association on Friday passed on a tender for one 54,000-tonne shipment of U.S. soybeans, local traders said.  </p>
<p>No retender date had been set, traders said.</p>
<p>The BSPA Kaohsiung division comprises Great Wall Enterprise, President Enterprise, Ttet Union and Tai Hwa Oil.</p>
<p>-- Taipei Newsroom (2-5080815)</p>
</text>
